WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.335
Lesson 0.4.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.172
Exchange account vs your own

00:00:04.172 --> 00:00:06.245
wallet: who holds the keys?.

00:00:06.245 --> 00:00:08.658
By the end of this lesson, you'll be able

00:00:08.658 --> 00:00:11.589
to understand custody and decide what stays on the

00:00:11.589 --> 00:00:14.060
exchange and what moves to your own wallet.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.650
Here's the plan.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.335
First, the key ideas.

00:00:18.335 --> 00:00:19.860
Then, your checklist.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.022
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:25.647
Who holds keys, The exchange, You.

00:00:25.647 --> 00:00:28.308
Recover if you forget password, Yes, with

00:00:28.308 --> 00:00:30.572
ID, Only with your seed phrase.

00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:32.285
Can be frozen, Yes, No.

00:00:32.285 --> 00:00:34.512
Can use DeFi, Limited, Yes.

00:00:34.512 --> 00:00:36.097
Your main risk, The company,

00:00:36.097 --> 00:00:37.627
Your own mistakes and scams.

00:00:38.927 --> 00:00:40.387
Here's your checklist.

00:00:40.387 --> 00:00:41.922
Do it now, for real.

00:00:41.922 --> 00:00:45.577
First, I can explain custodial vs self-custody.

00:00:45.577 --> 00:00:48.352
Next, I know my seed phrase is the wallet.

00:00:48.352 --> 00:00:50.746
And finally, I know an address is safe

00:00:50.746 --> 00:00:52.955
to share and a seed phrase never is.

00:00:54.255 --> 00:00:55.465
Question 1.

00:00:55.465 --> 00:00:57.920
What does "not your keys, not your coins" mean?

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.945
The answer: If someone else holds the keys, you

00:01:04.945 --> 00:01:07.115
depend on them to give your crypto back.

00:01:08.415 --> 00:01:09.660
Question 2.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.955
Is your crypto stored inside your wallet app?

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:18.910
The answer: No. It's on the blockchain.

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:21.115
The wallet holds the keys that control it.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.685
Question 3.

00:01:23.685 --> 00:01:25.060
Which can you share: your

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:26.540
address or your seed phrase?

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.705
The answer: Your address.

00:01:32.705 --> 00:01:34.045
Never the seed phrase.

00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:37.860
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.113
Next up, Lesson 0.5: Setting up

00:01:40.113 --> 00:01:42.225
your wallet and backing it up.
